{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1278383-reading-resources","id":1278383,"title":"Reading resources","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-03T12:43:46-08:00","id":1278383,"title":"Reading resources","content":"So there's obviously lots of fun fiction out there about the gods and other myths. But what resources do people like to use for information about the myths themselves, non-fiction? Any particular websites to give some more info, or any books people like? Most of my knowledge is limited to Greek/Roman mythology and some Norse and Egyptian stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T06:15:15-08:00","id":1278558,"title":"","content":"For me, getting into world mythology usually starts with using one of the Handbook of ____ Mythology books. The entries in those books are usually comprehensive. They don't go too in-depth into the characters and legends.<br /> <br /> Sacred-Texts.com has a lot of primary sources regarding religion and mythology. In my opinion, most books about non-Western religions are really old so I'd peruse certain translated works with caution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T10:29:19-08:00","id":1278627,"title":"","content":"I'm going to check out that site today! Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T11:38:13-08:00","id":1278650,"title":"","content":"Careful, though, the texts there are by nature very out of date. Some of the translations still hold up - for a lot of the Hindu stuff, there simply are no more recent ones, and taking into account the notes, the Eddic stuff is pretty solid as well - but others are a disaster - e.g. the Kojiki translation rendering the naughty passages in Latin because Victorian sensibilities. So with <i>Sacred Texts</i> as much as with everything else, it really depends on what culture you're interested in and what has been done about them. If you tell me anything you're particularly interested in, I could maybe point you to trustworthy websites and accesible books for that. Otherwise, here is a little reading list of scholarly titles I compiled a while ago - not necessarily &quot;must-reads&quot;, but a number of titles I personally found interesting and instructive.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ElxPpuOIIlC2WksRQA88op0CZdl8JRwe/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ElxPpuOIIlC2WksRQA88op0CZdl8JRwe/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ElxPpuOIIlC2WksRQA88op0CZdl8JRwe/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ElxPpuOIIlC2WksRQA88op0CZdl8JRwe/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}